## Page structure (home `/`)

Hero → About me → Work experience → Education → Side projects → Skills → Know me better

- **Work experience** = basics only: role, company, period, one-line `summary`, `stack` chips. Detailed bullets (`highlights`) appear only on `/resume`. Do not list company projects (Selangkah Plus, SCMS, SDMS, etc.) as portfolio cards.
- **Education** includes university/SIG activities (`universityProjects` in `education.ts`)
- **Side projects** = the owner’s self-built mini versions of each previous employer’s work, made with open data (e.g. Puncak Tegap → interactive GIS map with standard mapping features). Content in `side-projects.ts`; show honest `status` (planned / in-progress / live)
- **Know me better** = personal, non-work content in `personal.ts`. Never invent hobbies or personal facts; empty lists stay hidden

## Content

- **Single source of truth:** `src/content/*.ts`; never duplicate copy in components
- Resume HTML: `/resume` from same content; PDF export is a later phase
- Work text: NDA-safe; sync from user’s resume markdown when they update it

## Layout

- **Shipped:** `/` = Motion (GSAP hero + scroll reveal) with the structure above
- Archive: `/style/classic`, `/style/bento` stay for the owner to compare; keep them on the same content. Layout switcher bar is visible for now; hide it before the site is called finished
- **Theme:** light + dark via `next-themes` (class on `html`); tokens in `globals.css`

## Roadmap (owner wants the website finished first)

1. Finish the website content and layout (current phase)
2. Side project demos, starting with the GIS map at `/demos/...`
3. Screenshots via `image` in `side-projects.ts` + files in `public/projects/` (redact sensitive data)
4. Final phase: hide layout switcher, SEO metadata, PDF resume, custom domain

